                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Miracle Fly is an indie action platformer developed and published by ElagoTech that distinguishes itself by building its entire gameplay around an unusual flying mechanic instead of the traditional run-and-jump formula. From the very beginning, it is clear that the game is designed for players who enjoy learning new systems rather than relying on familiar controls. While the initial adjustment period may feel demanding, the game gradually rewards persistence with a satisfying movement system that becomes increasingly enjoyable as players develop better control and precision.\n\nThe heart of the experience lies in navigating more than one hundred handcrafted stages that combine platforming, environmental hazards, and puzzle-like challenges. Every level introduces new layouts or obstacle combinations that require careful timing and thoughtful movement instead of simple reflexes alone. The unconventional flight controls encourage players to think differently about positioning, momentum, and navigation, making even straightforward sections feel distinct from those found in conventional platformers. As the difficulty steadily increases, each completed stage provides a genuine sense of accomplishment without feeling unfair once the mechanics are understood.\n\nRather than presenting a story-heavy adventure, Miracle Fly focuses on creating a cheerful and imaginative atmosphere within its Dream World setting. The colorful anime-inspired art style gives every stage plenty of visual charm, while the character and enemy designs reinforce the game's playful personality. Boss encounters add welcome variety by challenging players to apply everything they have learned throughout the earlier stages. Combined with an energetic soundtrack and bright presentation, these encounters help maintain a fun and lighthearted tone even as the gameplay becomes more demanding.\n\nReplay value is another strong aspect of the package. Completing the main adventure unlocks New Game+, allowing players to revisit the campaign with different characters and fresh objectives. Steam Achievements, Trading Cards, Cloud support, and online Leaderboards provide additional incentives for players who enjoy chasing completion or competing for better performance. Since the game's hardware requirements remain modest, it is also accessible to players using older systems, making it easy for a broad audience to experience without requiring high-end equipment.\n\nMiracle Fly's greatest achievement is its willingness to take creative risks. Its distinctive movement system sets it apart from countless other indie platformers, giving it an identity that feels genuinely original. At the same time, that uniqueness may not appeal to everyone. Players expecting immediate accessibility or a narrative-driven adventure could find the learning curve and gameplay-first design less appealing. However, those who enjoy mastering unconventional mechanics and overcoming progressively more demanding platforming challenges are likely to appreciate what the game offers.\n\nOverall, Miracle Fly succeeds as an imaginative indie platformer that rewards patience with engaging gameplay, varied level design, appealing visuals, and worthwhile replayability. Although its unconventional controls may discourage some newcomers during the opening stages, players who commit to learning the mechanics will discover a creative and enjoyable experience that stands out within the genre.\n\nRating: 8/10",
